    {
      "id": "claim_e7f14b5b6c7c450ea415e594db619189",
      "statement": "Cell lifecycle states are resident (active/idle), hibernated (dormant but keeping hibernatable WebSockets on its node), and inactive (bucket-only); internally these are the core Phase machine from Inactive through cold-activation phases to Resident, celld 'evict' produces Dormant rather than unowned, and a cell keeps no memory across transitions so the constructor reruns on each cold event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L100-L135",
