      "id": "claim_86aa12f7dde34d3d9f6444d4e7f51167",
      "statement": "Eviction either releases ownership (any node may take it, which is how a loaded node sheds load) or keeps it sticky (same-node wake renames the local snapshot); a shutdown handoff proves a batch durable, publishes an L9 full snapshot when possible, releases the record, and asks a compatible peer to adopt the cell while it stays dormant rather than pre-restoring runtimes.",
